### Match commands -> POST /matches/{matchId}/events
### Set matchId from the CreateMatch.http response, then run blocks top-down.
### Every MatchCommand is wired in MatchService.handle: lifecycle, scoring,
### discipline, penalties, VAR and added time. Success is 202 Accepted.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@matchId = c4aec2c2-a189-4342-a1f4-0339ef54bf27

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### HAPPY PATH: SCHEDULED -> IN_PROGRESS -> HALF_TIME -> IN_PROGRESS -> COMPLETED
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1. Kick off. Expects 202. Status SCHEDULED -> IN_PROGRESS, scores set to 0-0.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_STARTED"
}

### 2. Half-time whistle. Expects 202. IN_PROGRESS -> HALF_TIME.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "FIRST_HALF_ENDED"
}

### 3. Second half kick off. Expects 202. HALF_TIME -> IN_PROGRESS.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "SECOND_HALF_STARTED"
}

### 4. Full time. Expects 202. IN_PROGRESS -> COMPLETED.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "FULL_TIME"
}

### 5. Verify the projection reflects the replayed events.
GET {{host}}/matches

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### ALTERNATE ENDINGS (use a fresh matchId for each)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 6. Postpone a match that never started. SCHEDULED -> POSTPONED.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_POSTPONED",
  "reason": "Waterlogged pitch"
}

### 7. Abandon a match already in progress. IN_PROGRESS -> ABANDONED.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_ABANDONED",
  "reason": "Floodlight failure",
  "minute": 63
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### GUARD RAILS: every one of these must be rejected by the aggregate
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 8. Start a match twice. Second call expects failure: "Match must be in scheduled state".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_STARTED"
}

### 9. Second half without a half-time first. Expects "match is not in half time".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "SECOND_HALF_STARTED"
}

### 10. Half-time whistle while at HALF_TIME. Expects "match is not in progress".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "FIRST_HALF_ENDED"
}

### 11. Full time on a COMPLETED / SCHEDULED match. Expects "match is not in progress".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "FULL_TIME"
}

### 12. Postpone a match that already kicked off. Expects "match must be scheduled".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_POSTPONED",
  "reason": "Too late to postpone"
}

### 13. Abandon a match that never started. Expects "match is not in progress".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_ABANDONED",
  "reason": "Crowd trouble outside the ground",
  "minute": 0
}

### 14. Unknown matchId. Expects "match not found".
POST {{host}}/matches/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_STARTED"
}

### 15. Unknown discriminator. Expects Jackson to reject the subtype.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "NOT_A_REAL_EVENT"
}

### 16. Missing discriminator. Expects Jackson to reject the missing type id.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "no type field"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### IN-PLAY COMMANDS: all handled. Each needs the match IN_PROGRESS, so run
### block 1 first. Scoring and cards also need the players to be on the pitch.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 17. Goal scored.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "GOAL_SCORED",
  "clubId": "0dffeae0-bb2e-4608-9e19-aa635e70adfc",
  "playerId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "minute": 48
}

### 18. Own goal.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "OWN_GOAL",
  "clubId": "7354f9c8-7885-4705-9fd0-e26fa6fa7997",
  "playerId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "minute": 31
}

### 19. Goal canceled. clubId is the club the cancelled goal was credited to,
### so for an own goal it is the conceding club's opponent.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "GOAL_CANCELED",
  "clubId": "0dffeae0-bb2e-4608-9e19-aa635e70adfc",
  "minute": 24
}

### 20. Yellow card.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "YELLOW_CARD_GIVEN",
  "clubId": "0dffeae0-bb2e-4608-9e19-aa635e70adfc",
  "playerId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "minute": 38
}

### 21. Second yellow for the same player as block 20. There is no
### SECOND_YELLOW_CARD command: send YELLOW_CARD_GIVEN again and the aggregate
### emits SECOND_YELLOW_CARD plus RED_CARD_GIVEN itself.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "YELLOW_CARD_GIVEN",
  "clubId": "0dffeae0-bb2e-4608-9e19-aa635e70adfc",
  "playerId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "minute": 71
}

### 22. Straight red.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "RED_CARD_GIVEN",
  "clubId": "7354f9c8-7885-4705-9fd0-e26fa6fa7997",
  "playerId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "minute": 74
}

### 23. Substitution.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "SUBSTITUTION",
  "clubId": "0dffeae0-bb2e-4608-9e19-aa635e70adfc",
  "playerOutId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111112",
  "playerInId": "44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444",
  "minute": 60
}

### 24. Penalty awarded.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "PENALTY_AWARDED",
  "clubId": "0dffeae0-bb2e-4608-9e19-aa635e70adfc",
  "minute": 78
}

### 25. Penalty scored.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "PENALTY_SCORED",
  "clubId": "0dffeae0-bb2e-4608-9e19-aa635e70adfc",
  "playerId": "44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444",
  "minute": 79
}

### 26. Penalty missed.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "PENALTY_MISSED",
  "clubId": "7354f9c8-7885-4705-9fd0-e26fa6fa7997",
  "playerId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "minute": 85
}

### 27. VAR check started. Opens a check; only one may be open at a time.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "VAR_CHECK_STARTED",
  "reason": "Possible penalty",
  "minute": 77
}

### 28. VAR decision. Closes the check opened in block 27. The decision is
### recorded as free text only: it emits no corrective event of its own, so
### cancelling a goal or awarding a penalty is a separate command.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "VAR_DECISION",
  "decision": "PENALTY_CONFIRMED",
  "minute": 78
}

### 29. Added time announced.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "ADDED_TIME_ANNOUNCED",
  "addedMinutes": 5
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### VALIDATION: @NotNull / @Min(0) / @NotBlank on the command records
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 30. Negative minute. Expects 400 from @Min(0).
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "GOAL_SCORED",
  "clubId": "0dffeae0-bb2e-4608-9e19-aa635e70adfc",
  "playerId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "minute": -1
}

### 31. Missing required clubId/playerId. Expects 400 from @NotNull.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "GOAL_SCORED",
  "minute": 12
}

### 32. Blank VAR decision. Expects 400 from @NotBlank.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "VAR_DECISION",
  "decision": "",
  "minute": 78
}

### 33. Blank VAR check reason. Expects 400 from @NotBlank.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "VAR_CHECK_STARTED",
  "reason": "",
  "minute": 77
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### VAR GUARD RAILS: an open check must be decided before play moves on
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 34. Decision with no check open. Expects "no var check is awaiting a decision".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "VAR_DECISION",
  "decision": "NO_OFFENCE",
  "minute": 78
}

### 35. Second check while one is open. Run block 27 first.
### Expects "a var check is awaiting a decision".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "VAR_CHECK_STARTED",
  "reason": "Possible offside",
  "minute": 78
}

### 36. Half-time whistle with a check still open. Run block 27 first.
### Expects "a var check is awaiting a decision". FULL_TIME and
### SECOND_HALF_STARTED are blocked the same way.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "FIRST_HALF_ENDED"
}
